Z||000000||85blackgt||07-04-2001||11:16 AM||||can i just was it with whose and some soap? i would like to armor all the rubber and whoses does this sound ok?<P>------------------<BR>I stick my head out the window,when its closed instead of air i get glass stuck into my head,the city's sounding i can't seem to stop the pounding, can't keep my thoughts from flying round, not sure  what im thinking about, i got SOUL DOUBT!!!- NOFX<P>1986 Fiero SE 2.8lv6||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||07-04-2001||12:13 PM||||You probably need something a bit stronger than dish soap. Simple Green or a citrus based cleaner work good as long as it's not baked hard.<P>Just make sure water can't get inside places it normally would not go. Mainly we worry about pressure washing... regular hoses won't hurt anything... (Do this on a cold motor. sudden cooling often starts cracks in the exhaust manifold(s).)||||reg||1
Z||000002||RacinRob||07-04-2001||02:25 PM||||I use engine degreaser and a little brush and that seems to do a good job. It tends to make the plastic parts look dry though.  I'm sure a little armorall would fix that.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Sootah||07-04-2001||02:34 PM||||A lot of carwash places have a tire and engine cleaner option on em'. Go there w/ a cool engine squrt some of the stuff all over in there, let it sit a bit and then rinse off with the final rinse thing (Its usually low pressure) May as well wash the rest of your car while your at it. Beware: As soon as you see the engine all clean and purdy you'll have to keep it that way.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||07-05-2001||08:58 AM||||try not to spray directly on relays, map, throttle body or distributor with lots of pressure. I did blow an alternator washing engine. I a firm believer in 'NEVER' using armor all on anything except my go cart tires.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Will||07-05-2001||10:20 AM||||If you want to protect your sensors while you wash, you might try ziplock bags and rubber bands on them.||||reg||1
